[{:db/id "q-85977/selection/657895b0b88e622794d55baf5a31e500e53ad77cf757ebbda809166ab399a9df" :answer/id #uuid "9381805b-ffb0-5b7f-b57f-b2faebadf8be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{4\\,500}{1-29{e}^{-900t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85977/selection/bfd654d5151b1cacb76412fafc7dde01478c82d95090213cbde415f22f70c647" :answer/id #uuid "77df335e-22ae-5204-8b78-e56937680d52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{4\\,500}{1+29{e}^{-900t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85977/selection/93a947012089fb576294a5fa5febda0cbd24a0a054a6b515ed141b58afe9c2bd" :answer/id #uuid "17a6d571-d5ca-5a1b-99bc-db8a3512506c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{4\\,500}{1+29{e}^{-90t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85977/selection/7768bf2c94f39c14ce32edba3e02f6d8642bae64e37777e22c421ec56e9da8eb" :answer/id #uuid "7fa3dde8-86c0-5e8b-b811-ddb7b69ce23a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{4\\,500}{1+150{e}^{-900t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85977/selection/32a73f74abbc6cbc523e81950aa154072b945f39cd1052b0b667fe5126795380" :answer/id #uuid "1ad7e000-9a43-586f-9040-0a3f8dc0336f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{3\\,000}{1-29{e}^{-900t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85977/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cde39490-7ba7-5a36-af6a-63005aac1168" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85977/selection/bfd654d5151b1cacb76412fafc7dde01478c82d95090213cbde415f22f70c647" :answer-field/choices ["q-85977/selection/657895b0b88e622794d55baf5a31e500e53ad77cf757ebbda809166ab399a9df" "q-85977/selection/bfd654d5151b1cacb76412fafc7dde01478c82d95090213cbde415f22f70c647" "q-85977/selection/93a947012089fb576294a5fa5febda0cbd24a0a054a6b515ed141b58afe9c2bd" "q-85977/selection/7768bf2c94f39c14ce32edba3e02f6d8642bae64e37777e22c421ec56e9da8eb" "q-85977/selection/32a73f74abbc6cbc523e81950aa154072b945f39cd1052b0b667fe5126795380"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85977" :question/id #uuid "9caecca5-59a6-5277-9b1d-c52fd8f94958" :question/math-academy-id "q-85977" :question/problem "The rate of growth of the bear population $P(t)$ in a certain forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.2P(4\\,500-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years. Find an expression for the bear population after $t$ years, given that there were $150$ bears initially." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.2,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=4\\,500.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{4\\,500}{1+C{e}^{-(4\\,500\\cdot 0.2)t}}=\\frac{4\\,500}{1+C{e}^{-900t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=150$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\,500}{1+C{e}^{-900\\cdot 0}} & =150 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{4\\,500}{150} \\\\ C & =30-1 \\\\  & =29.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{4\\,500}{1+29{e}^{-900t}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85977/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e71ba74-f952-56ef-885c-a32c4a4aec20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85977"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119861/selection/a8af11b3b7bbcc2414a7f126dfd3f81ca090832b102097a1bd02c1380391f645" :answer/id #uuid "e453d900-273f-5a1e-851e-0d6d5a484e2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{130}{1+25{e}^{-0.009t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119861/selection/e7442460046a2d3ed1a8e676c185df2b6e4227c166ca5015d97c8d79fc610a8b" :answer/id #uuid "797ca0e7-6bec-5dab-9b05-d0a0c20f2ad7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{130}{1+25{e}^{-1.17t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119861/selection/9fb5fc3232d439427c0504f1be154b28d723ddf39f07adbe17e1a8d2f103312e" :answer/id #uuid "391985b4-fcd1-50ad-890f-1b7e26744141" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{25}{1+{e}^{-t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119861/selection/43c50a39a9e9f066f37c1eca5c95ccfbc2cddd0006f35c8d4f6f80be0f69572b" :answer/id #uuid "8912babc-6e4b-5f3e-912d-6a0065743b20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{25}{1+{e}^{-0.009t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119861/selection/63df285d8de315a1a1c979e44050c49f019b4afd232e69c71c48f5ec62eda8d9" :answer/id #uuid "1e992a9d-587d-5289-ae53-0e7d820fc4e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{5}{1+25{e}^{-1.17t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119861/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "de450828-f588-5f1a-88f1-da16f9577e9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119861/selection/e7442460046a2d3ed1a8e676c185df2b6e4227c166ca5015d97c8d79fc610a8b" :answer-field/choices ["q-119861/selection/a8af11b3b7bbcc2414a7f126dfd3f81ca090832b102097a1bd02c1380391f645" "q-119861/selection/e7442460046a2d3ed1a8e676c185df2b6e4227c166ca5015d97c8d79fc610a8b" "q-119861/selection/9fb5fc3232d439427c0504f1be154b28d723ddf39f07adbe17e1a8d2f103312e" "q-119861/selection/43c50a39a9e9f066f37c1eca5c95ccfbc2cddd0006f35c8d4f6f80be0f69572b" "q-119861/selection/63df285d8de315a1a1c979e44050c49f019b4afd232e69c71c48f5ec62eda8d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119861" :question/id #uuid "2ca1449f-8949-5519-8f98-ed37dccf1a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-119861" :question/problem "The rate of growth in the number of fishes $P(t)$ with a fungal infection in a certain pond is jointly proportional to the number of fishes that have been infected at time $t$ and the number that have not been infected. If the constant of proportionality is $0.009$ and the carrying capacity is $130,$ then find an expression for the number of fishes with fungal infection, given that there were $5$ fishes infected initially." :question/worked-solution "Since the growth rate of infected fishes is *jointly* proportional to the number of fishes that have been infected at time $t,$ and the number that have not, the number of infected fishes follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.009,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=130.$ Therefore, the growth of the number of fishes with fungal infection is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.009P(130-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{130}{1+C{e}^{-(130\\cdot 0.009)t}}=\\frac{130}{1+C{e}^{-1.17t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=5$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{130}{1+C{e}^{-1.17\\cdot 0}} & =5 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{130}{5} \\\\ C & =26-1 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(t)=\\frac{130}{1+25{e}^{-1.17t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119861/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e71ba74-f952-56ef-885c-a32c4a4aec20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119861"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353253/field-1/626b4948e1e0e3940807231361807f561f1f70b2fbee6f9081bb4f2411683249" :answer/id #uuid "9d807166-1d92-5d35-8b97-350a0171ca76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7e^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353253/field-1/c8f1d887d148882c069de8d3655c4be2f6f0320103e3d42bb5ce5b05ea91b768" :answer/id #uuid "b5b391eb-74f1-59d0-9560-7d57c357dc98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7e^{-0.005t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353253/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "10162ae4-12f0-5d53-a516-997edbc6bdb9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353253/field-1/626b4948e1e0e3940807231361807f561f1f70b2fbee6f9081bb4f2411683249" :answer-field/choices ["q-353253/field-1/626b4948e1e0e3940807231361807f561f1f70b2fbee6f9081bb4f2411683249" "q-353253/field-1/c8f1d887d148882c069de8d3655c4be2f6f0320103e3d42bb5ce5b05ea91b768"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353253" :question/id #uuid "d3bdf0d0-1ee1-5303-bb41-ac3247396350" :question/math-academy-id "q-353253" :question/problem "The growth rate of the number of residents using a new fitness app, $P(t),$ in a small town is jointly proportional to the number of residents using the app at time $t,$ measured in months, and the difference between the town’s maximum potential users and the number of residents currently using the app.\n\nGiven that the constant of proportionality is $0.005$ and the maximum potential number of users is $800,$ find an expression for the number of residents using the app after $t$ months, given that there were $100$ users initially.\n\n| $P(t)\\,=\\,\\,$ | $800$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1\\,+\\,$ {{field-1}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Since the number of residents using the app grows at a rate that is *jointly* proportional to the number of residents using the app at time $t$ and the difference between the maximum potential number of users and the number currently using the app, the number of residents using the app follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.005,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=800.$ Therefore, the growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.005\\,P(800-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{800}{1+C{e}^{-(800\\cdot 0.005)t}}=\\frac{800}{1+C{e}^{-4t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=100$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{800}{1+C{e}^{-4\\cdot 0}} & =100 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{800}{100} \\\\ C & =8-1 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{800}{1+7{e}^{-4t}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353253/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e71ba74-f952-56ef-885c-a32c4a4aec20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353253"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83875/selection/541cfac908e6293426b9f70602e38facc6008f23eda45a478e5251980ebaea16" :answer/id #uuid "f5667cf1-af77-58a2-b72c-d6f61340dfa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+5{e}^{-0.5t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83875/selection/c3e172d0479fcccee19b3860e91e54f2d8d4fa74f0507d727fb3dcabcba53ffb" :answer/id #uuid "27d2d6b5-cb2e-5d17-8073-8869cb3e29f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+5{e}^{-0.2t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83875/selection/d132e0d1f95f93229600c49b15c915e689ca12366a04cf7d75bcb70f1d0e77ac" :answer/id #uuid "e227422d-dcc6-5b54-9f4b-d9f22cfdb811" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+4{e}^{-2t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83875/selection/7ce5949611ff0940149f71e4e964d237ed52ae160406864933d886378593cbd8" :answer/id #uuid "5b2bb338-8323-5a37-85df-4d3475e72dfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-0.5t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83875/selection/8adf2ad15b4daae89d684f6f92e6bd5ddb67f7d4393e8b4864ee84b5ccfce27a" :answer/id #uuid "e93486dd-58e8-5462-8e07-7e15bf46c002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+4{e}^{-0.1t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83875/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bde01042-6422-5410-8ce9-f190084bf700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83875/selection/7ce5949611ff0940149f71e4e964d237ed52ae160406864933d886378593cbd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-83875/selection/541cfac908e6293426b9f70602e38facc6008f23eda45a478e5251980ebaea16" "q-83875/selection/c3e172d0479fcccee19b3860e91e54f2d8d4fa74f0507d727fb3dcabcba53ffb" "q-83875/selection/d132e0d1f95f93229600c49b15c915e689ca12366a04cf7d75bcb70f1d0e77ac" "q-83875/selection/7ce5949611ff0940149f71e4e964d237ed52ae160406864933d886378593cbd8" "q-83875/selection/8adf2ad15b4daae89d684f6f92e6bd5ddb67f7d4393e8b4864ee84b5ccfce27a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83875" :question/id #uuid "deb24d9c-7f82-577b-9801-7cd591df4750" :question/math-academy-id "q-83875" :question/problem "The growth rate of the mouse population $P(t)$ in a certain field is jointly proportional to the mouse population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the field's carrying capacity and the mouse population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,062\\,5$ and the carrying capacity is $8\\,000,$ then find an expression for the mouse population after $t$ years, given that there were $1\\,000$ mice in the field initially." :question/worked-solution "Since the mouse population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the mouse population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the mouse population, the mouse population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,062\\,5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=8\\,000.$ Therefore, the mouse population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,062\\,5P(8\\,000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(8\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,062\\,5)t}}=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.5t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=1\\,000$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.5\\cdot 0}} & =1\\,000 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{8\\,000}{1\\,000} \\\\ C & =8-1 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-0.5t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83875/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e71ba74-f952-56ef-885c-a32c4a4aec20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83875"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83868/selection/5eccd793030dd77b6bcaa9859279be61e616e3d86875728122defafab295ed9e" :answer/id #uuid "a23ab289-7408-5f72-b763-93b399d59fd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{10\\,000}{1+4{e}^{-2t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83868/selection/75c8e18b5fecdb2a8f247b40fa770ec8f36faa25b3135c7f2c01ea017902180a" :answer/id #uuid "701d448d-ecf2-59e0-b307-8df5d49a1e68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{10\\,000}{1+5{e}^{-0.2t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83868/selection/60da2a9fcb9d0ea06d15a4f250473bc4d62cc769eba11a094e6cca56ac1bd7d8" :answer/id #uuid "d9dc8695-230d-5236-b5b3-c467a3463d25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{10\\,000}{1+4{e}^{-0.1t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83868/selection/a2e6943ceb3c7a4536b53ecb85c528058f997a8c32550a6c79e11ea9544c8ca3" :answer/id #uuid "0488013f-329e-55ab-abc0-d8cf0acfcb5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{10\\,000}{1+9{e}^{-0.2t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83868/selection/ecd428d98e8e9a22f8af595ac9868c2ef896d64cd39b519f48c47c046c6abe52" :answer/id #uuid "963cd396-bb73-5c75-ba38-1371f63c5389" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{10\\,000}{1+5{e}^{-2t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83868/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "413a0b70-8446-552e-bb92-a85faa7bb468" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83868/selection/a2e6943ceb3c7a4536b53ecb85c528058f997a8c32550a6c79e11ea9544c8ca3" :answer-field/choices ["q-83868/selection/5eccd793030dd77b6bcaa9859279be61e616e3d86875728122defafab295ed9e" "q-83868/selection/75c8e18b5fecdb2a8f247b40fa770ec8f36faa25b3135c7f2c01ea017902180a" "q-83868/selection/60da2a9fcb9d0ea06d15a4f250473bc4d62cc769eba11a094e6cca56ac1bd7d8" "q-83868/selection/a2e6943ceb3c7a4536b53ecb85c528058f997a8c32550a6c79e11ea9544c8ca3" "q-83868/selection/ecd428d98e8e9a22f8af595ac9868c2ef896d64cd39b519f48c47c046c6abe52"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83868" :question/id #uuid "2189f101-13f3-56fd-94db-1f1071ee6a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-83868" :question/problem "The growth rate of the crab population $P(t)$ in a certain river is jointly proportional to the crab population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the river's carrying capacity and the crab population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,02$ and the carrying capacity is $10\\,000,$ then find an expression for the crab population after $t$ years, given that there were $1\\,000$ crab in the river initially." :question/worked-solution "Since the crab population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the crab population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the crab population, the crab population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,02,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=10\\,000.$ Therefore, the crab population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,02P(10\\,000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{10\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(10\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,02t)}}=\\frac{10\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.2t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=1\\,000$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.2\\cdot 0}} & =1\\,000 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{10\\,000}{1\\,000} \\\\ C & =10-1 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(t)=\\frac{10\\,000}{1+9{e}^{-0.2t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83868/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e71ba74-f952-56ef-885c-a32c4a4aec20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83868"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-83771"] :question/problem "The growth rate of the squirrel population $P(t)$ in a certain forest is jointly proportional to the squirrel population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the forest's carrying capacity and the squirrel population. The constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,01$ and the carrying capacity is $5000.$ How many squirrels will there be in the forest after $10$ years given that there were $4000$ squirrels initially? Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "Since the squirrel population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the squirrel population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the squirrel population, the squirrel population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,01,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=5000.$ Therefore, the squirrel population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,01P(5000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{5000}{1+C{e}^{-(5000\\cdot 0.000\\,01)t}}=\\frac{5000}{1+C{e}^{-0.05t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=4000$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =4000 \\\\ \\frac{5000}{1+C{e}^{-0.05(0)}} & =4000 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ C & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{5000}{1+0.25{e}^{-0.05\\cdot t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=10$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10) & =\\frac{5000}{1+0.25{e}^{-0.05\\cdot 10}} \\\\  & ≈4342.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-347875/field-1/3d4ded9292fea73f913626717a590a61b202db844b385080bb074e1c5760c1d1" :answer/id #uuid "0022dcba-6cad-574b-b71e-4fa8ab87afaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "548" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347875/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "746cee96-5e9f-5474-9c16-10527f2d168e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347875/field-1/3d4ded9292fea73f913626717a590a61b202db844b385080bb074e1c5760c1d1" :answer-field/choices ["q-347875/field-1/3d4ded9292fea73f913626717a590a61b202db844b385080bb074e1c5760c1d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347875" :question/id #uuid "ebc94644-35a7-5ccd-b4dd-ea6583f0712d" :question/math-academy-id "q-347875" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of rabbits on a particular island follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.2P-0.0002{P}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. If there were $400$ rabbits on the island initially, how many rabbits inhabited the island after $3$ years? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nAfter $3$ years, approximately\n{{field-1}} rabbits inhabited the island." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.2P-0.0002{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.0002P(1000-P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.0002,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=1000.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{1000}{1+C{e}^{-(1000\\cdot 0.0002)t}}=\\frac{1000}{1+C{e}^{-0.2t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=400$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1000}{1+C{e}^{-0.2(0)}} & =400 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{1000}{400} \\\\ C & =2.5-1 \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{1000}{1+1.5{e}^{-0.2t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=3$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3) & =\\frac{1000}{1+1.5{e}^{-0.2(3)}} \\\\  & ≈548.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $3$ years, approximately $548$ rabbits inhabited the island." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-347875/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18af80e5-cd0f-5a1d-b299-2956fd886c5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347875"] :db/ensure [:knowledg