60045fe64c" :question/math-academy-id "q-85978" :question/problem "The growth rate of the deer population $P(t)$ in a certain forest is jointly proportional to the deer population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the forest's carrying capacity and the deer population. The constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,03$ and the carrying capacity is $9000.$ How many deers will there be in the forest after $8$ years given that there were $1800$ deers initially? Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "Since the deer population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the deer population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the deer population, the deer population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,03,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=9000.$ Therefore, the deer population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,03P(9000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{9000}{1+C{e}^{-(9000\\cdot 0.000\\,03)t}}=\\frac{9000}{1+C{e}^{-0.27t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=1800$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =1800 \\\\ \\frac{9000}{1+C{e}^{-0.27(0)}} & =1800 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{9000}{1800} \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{9000}{1+4{e}^{-0.27\\cdot t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=8$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8) & =\\frac{9000}{1+4{e}^{-0.27\\cdot 8}} \\\\  & ≈6159.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-85978/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18af80e5-cd0f-5a1d-b299-2956fd886c5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85978"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120253/selection/69d2c9e9a55fada91468e5d2dc0a7ca466262b59ef072849a8fd9f008b298132" :answer/id #uuid "54a2609e-7724-5d06-8c34-e5b59cc61ae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,638" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120253/selection/59d019059fcf81ecc2152bc3a103cf67aa691b8b2a42ce7146857e88de0edb36" :answer/id #uuid "bc5a3bd2-32fd-50bc-b18d-9843dbda43a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120253/selection/abf617104680fb192056e1c9f657e38a6884fc6ae8997b265db9226e7ed0dccf" :answer/id #uuid "18236403-e1d5-5d60-adba-83c15e215827" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "99" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120253/selection/9f3c8c0bb575b753c9720d401d8e1fcdc4c07c51aade593b7e5319e5b10fc67d" :answer/id #uuid "6ecd2d6f-e151-5d0b-ba28-6a81c1980514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120253/selection/5e1d4db76fc4b06a9708bac75c1002b8bf1fbf8beccb8ff6e0e1f17aaf87a3af" :answer/id #uuid "8f6b953d-3ac6-54e5-a1c4-5579ce19b0ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80\\,296" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120253/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "49671687-4a8b-5d56-906f-715ca3c0205c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120253/selection/5e1d4db76fc4b06a9708bac75c1002b8bf1fbf8beccb8ff6e0e1f17aaf87a3af" :answer-field/choices ["q-120253/selection/69d2c9e9a55fada91468e5d2dc0a7ca466262b59ef072849a8fd9f008b298132" "q-120253/selection/59d019059fcf81ecc2152bc3a103cf67aa691b8b2a42ce7146857e88de0edb36" "q-120253/selection/abf617104680fb192056e1c9f657e38a6884fc6ae8997b265db9226e7ed0dccf" "q-120253/selection/9f3c8c0bb575b753c9720d401d8e1fcdc4c07c51aade593b7e5319e5b10fc67d" "q-120253/selection/5e1d4db76fc4b06a9708bac75c1002b8bf1fbf8beccb8ff6e0e1f17aaf87a3af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120253" :question/id #uuid "01e090ea-18cf-5d07-9563-7039d4d1d497" :question/math-academy-id "q-120253" :question/problem "The growth rate in the number $P(t)$ of files infected with a virus in a computer is jointly proportional to the number of infected files at time $t,$ measured in hours, and the difference between the computer's carrying capacity and the number of infected files. The constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,005$ and the carrying capacity is $100\\,000.$ How many files will have the virus after $12$ hours given that there were $1000$ files with the virus initially? Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "Since the number of files infected with the virus' growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the number of infected files at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the number of infected files, the number of files infected with the virus follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,005,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=100\\,000.$ Therefore, the growth of the number of files infected with the virus is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,005P(100\\,000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{100\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(100\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,005)t}}=\\frac{100\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.5t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=1000$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =1000 \\\\ \\frac{100\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.5(0)}} & =1000 \\\\ 1+C & =100 \\\\ C & =99.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{100\\,000}{1+99{e}^{-0.5\\cdot t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=12$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(12) & =\\frac{100\\,000}{1+99{e}^{-0.5\\cdot 12}} \\\\  & ≈80\\,296.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-120253/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18af80e5-cd0f-5a1d-b299-2956fd886c5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120253"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83895/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c3675c40-3e87-56e8-bdc6-7450f2fbacbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83895/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "f2270adc-ac34-5a91-96c4-38b5616bdc6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83895/selection/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer/id #uuid "58565b70-0e3b-53a1-bcf3-dccaa82d446b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83895/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "1f4192d8-01d9-5fee-a36b-a00545f09a48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83895/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9" :answer/id #uuid "6b5d7d5e-b28c-5e87-884c-92e31f19694d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83895/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ccdf6183-a13b-5676-b67b-e64e469c9685" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83895/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-83895/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-83895/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-83895/selection/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" "q-83895/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" "q-83895/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83895" :question/id #uuid "cc96676a-202b-5c2e-ae13-566e31d66cbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-83895" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of turtles on a particular island follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.05P-0.000\\,5{P}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. If there were $5$ turtles on the island initially, how many turtles inhabited the island after $11$ years? Round you answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.05P-0.000\\,5{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.000\\,5P(100-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=100.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-(100\\cdot 0.000\\,5)t}}=\\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-0.05t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=5$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-0.05(0)}} & =5 \\\\ 1+C & =20 \\\\ C & =19\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{100}{1+19{e}^{-0.05t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=11$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(11) & =\\frac{100}{1+19{e}^{-0.05(11)}} \\\\  & ≈8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $11$ years, approximately $8$ turtles inhabited the island." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83895/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18af80e5-cd0f-5a1d-b299-2956fd886c5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83895"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7408"] :question/problem "The rate of growth of the panda population $P(t)$ in a particular forest follows the logistic growth model is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} P}{\\mathrm{d} t} = 0.001\\,25 P(800-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the beginning of the observations. Find an expression for the panda population after $t$ years, given that there were $400$ pandas initially." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} P}{\\mathrm{d} t} = kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k > 0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a > P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t) = \\dfrac{a}{1+Ce^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.001\\,25,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=800.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\nP(t) \n= \\dfrac{800}{1+Ce^{-(800\\cdot 0.001\\,25)t}}= \\dfrac{800}{1+Ce^{-t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=400$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{800}{1+C{e}^{-0}} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{800}{1+C} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{1+C}{800} & =\\frac{1}{400} \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{800}{400} \\\\ C & =2-1 \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the panda population is given by\n\n$$\nP(t)= \\dfrac{800}{1+e^{-t}} .\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7407"] :question/problem "The growth rate of the hare population $P(t)$ in a particular forest is jointly proportional to the hare population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the forest's carrying capacity and the hare population. The constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,01$ and the carrying capacity is $10\\,000.$ How many hares will there be in the forest after $7$ years given that there were $2\\,500$ hares initially? Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "Since the hare population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the hare population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the hare population, the hare population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} P}{\\mathrm{d} t} = kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k > 0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a > P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t) = \\dfrac{a}{1+Ce^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality $k=0.000\\,01,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=10\\,000.$ Therefore, the hare population is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d} P}{\\mathrm{d} t} = 0.000\\,01 P(10\\,000-P) .\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t) \n= \\dfrac{10\\,000}{1+Ce^{-(10\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,01)t}}= \\dfrac{10\\,000}{1+Ce^{-0.1t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=2\\,500$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =2\\,500 \\\\ \\frac{10\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.1(0)}} & =2\\,500 \\\\ \\frac{10\\,000}{1+C} & =2\\,500 \\\\ \\frac{1+C}{10\\,000} & =\\frac{1}{2\\,500} \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{10\\,000}{2\\,500} \\\\ 1+C & =4 \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t) = \\frac{10\\,000}{1+3 e^{-0.1 t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of hares in the forest after $7$ years, we substitute $t=7$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(7) & =\\frac{10\\,000}{1+3{e}^{-0.1\\cdot 7}} \\\\  & ≈4\\,016.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
